---
code: K0010
title: Extern Without Return Type
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, extern, ffi, function, return-type]
description: "'extern' function declaration is missing a return type"
---

An `extern` function declaration requires an explicit return type annotation so the compiler knows the foreign function's calling convention and ABI signature.

## Example

This error occurs when an `extern` function is declared without a return type:

```kura
extern fn log_message(msg: String)
```

It also occurs when an `extern` function has no parameters and omits the return type:

```kura
extern fn flush_frame()
```

## Solution

Add an explicit return type annotation (such as `Int` or `String` for functions that do not return a value):

```kura
extern fn get_timestamp(): Int
```
